1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,500
中国空间站里，
Inside China's space station,

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,210
造出了人类已知最冷的人造物质。
scientists made the coldest man-made stuff we know of.

3
00:00:04,210 --> 00:00:05,670
九点七皮开尔文，
Nine point seven picokelvin.

4
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:07,800
离绝对零度只差一丁点。
A hair above absolute zero.

5
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,200
比宇宙深空还冷，
Colder than deep space,

6
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,450
我们算了一下，冷了大约两千八百亿倍。
about two hundred eighty billion times colder, by our math.

7
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:14,990
十一月六日，论文登上《科学》，
On November sixth the paper came out in Science,

8
00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:16,290
一下子刷屏了。
and it was everywhere.

9
00:00:16,290 --> 00:00:17,870
今天的烧脑问题：
Today's brain teaser:

10
00:00:17,870 --> 00:00:20,940
为啥非得跑到太空，才能这么冷？
why go all the way to space to get this cold?

11
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,750
认识主角：一颗铷原子，
Meet our hero: a rubidium atom,

12
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:23,370
小铷。
Little Rubi.

13
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:24,640
温度到底是啥？
What is temperature, really?

14
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:26,570
就是原子乱跑的快慢。
It's how fast atoms jitter around.

15
00:00:26,570 --> 00:00:29,000
室温下，小铷每秒跑好几百米，
At room temperature, Rubi zooms hundreds of meters a second,

16
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,510
跟飞机差不多快。
about as fast as a jet.

17
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:32,260
降到九点七皮开尔文，
At nine point seven picokelvin,

18
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:34,820
它每秒只挪大约零点零五毫米。
it creeps about five hundredths of a millimeter a second.

19
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:36,430
比蜗牛还慢二十来倍，
Twenty times slower than a snail,

20
00:00:36,430 --> 00:00:38,320
这是我们按公式估算的。
by our own estimate.

21
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,680
怎么让原子慢下来？
How do you slow atoms down?

22
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,610
第一步，用激光“刹车”。
Step one: laser brakes.

23
00:00:41,610 --> 00:00:44,120
好几束激光从四面八方照过来，
Lasers shine in from every side,

24
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:46,920
像迎面扔来的乒乓球，越跑越慢。
like ping pong balls hitting you head on.

25
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:48,390
第二步，蒸发冷却，
Step two: evaporative cooling,

26
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:50,150
跟你吹热汤一个道理。
the same trick as blowing on hot soup.

27
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:52,360
汤里最“热”的分子先飞走，
The hottest molecules fly off first,

28
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:53,680
剩下的就凉了。
and what's left cools down.

29
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:55,720
原子关在光做的“碗”里，
The atoms sit in a bowl made of light.

30
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:58,570
碗边一点点放低，跑得快的就溜了。
Lower the rim, and the fast ones escape.

31
00:00:58,570 --> 00:01:01,340
反转一：碗边越低，剩下的越冷。
Twist one: the lower the rim, the colder the rest.

32
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:03,670
可在地面上，碗边放不低。
But on Earth, you can't lower it far.

33
00:01:03,670 --> 00:01:05,490
因为重力把原子往下拽，
Gravity drags the atoms down.

34
00:01:05,490 --> 00:01:07,930
碗一放低，它们从底下漏光了。
Lower the bowl, and they spill out the bottom.

35
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:09,690
就像斜坡上放一碗汤，
Like a bowl of soup on a slope:

36
00:01:09,690 --> 00:01:12,090
碗边一低，汤先从下面洒了。
lower the rim, and it spills downhill.

37
00:01:12,090 --> 00:01:14,640
在空间站里，大家一起自由下落，
On the space station, everything falls together,

38
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,630
原子感觉不到“往下”。
so the atoms feel no 'down'.

39
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:18,650
碗边可以放得很低很低，
The rim can go really, really low,

40
00:01:18,650 --> 00:01:20,250
原子还乖乖待着。
and the atoms still stay put.

41
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:22,080
反转二：还有更狠的一招，
Twist two: there's an even sneakier move,

42
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:23,570
叫“非绝热扩散”。
called non-adiabatic expansion.

43
00:01:23,570 --> 00:01:26,260
简单说，让原子云在更大的碗里散开，
Basically, let the cloud spread out into a bigger bowl,

44
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:27,650
又降了一截温度。
and it cools down another notch.

45
00:01:27,650 --> 00:01:29,470
就像打开一罐汽水，
Like opening a can of soda:

46
00:01:29,470 --> 00:01:32,010
气一冲出来，罐口凉飕飕。
the gas rushes out, and the can top feels cold.

47
00:01:32,010 --> 00:01:35,570
二零二二年，国际空间站做到五十二皮开尔文；
In twenty twenty two, the International Space Station hit fifty two picokelvin.

48
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:37,220
这次降到了九点七。
This one hit nine point seven.

49
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:38,290
低了五倍多，
More than five times lower,

50
00:01:38,290 --> 00:01:40,180
而且能盯着看七秒钟。
and they could watch it for seven seconds.

51
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:41,370
反转三，最难：
Twist three, the hardest part:

52
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:45,050
这台“冰箱”在地面上有二十立方米、十吨重。
on the ground this freezer filled twenty cubic meters and weighed ten tons.

53
00:01:45,050 --> 00:01:47,560
科学家把它塞进零点七立方米、
They squeezed it into a cabinet of point seven cubic meters,

54
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:49,110
半吨重的实验柜。
weighing half a ton.

55
00:01:49,110 --> 00:01:51,000
从二零一一年论证开始，
From the first plans in twenty eleven,

56
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,500
做了大约十五年。
it took about fifteen years.

57
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:53,950
里面只用了五克铷，
It started with just five grams of rubidium,

58
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:55,670
比一枚一元硬币还轻。
lighter than a coin.

59
00:01:55,670 --> 00:01:56,750
这么冷有啥用？
Why so cold?

60
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:59,030
原子越慢，越能当精确的尺子。
The slower the atoms, the better they work as rulers.

61
00:01:59,030 --> 00:02:02,130
能做更准的原子干涉仪和量子传感器，
Better atom interferometers and quantum sensors,

62
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:04,430
测地球重力、帮飞船导航。
to map Earth's gravity and help navigation.

63
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:05,740
还能研究暗物质，
They may even help hunt dark matter

64
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:07,830
模拟宇宙刚诞生时的样子。
and mimic the early universe.

65
00:02:07,830 --> 00:02:10,270
友情提示：最冷的是这团原子云，
Fine print: only this tiny atom cloud is that cold.

66
00:02:10,270 --> 00:02:12,020
空间站里一点也不冷。
The station itself is comfy.

67
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:14,010
两千八百亿倍、比蜗牛慢，
The two hundred eighty billion and the snail

68
00:02:14,010 --> 00:02:16,630
都是我们自己估算的，算个大概。
are our own rough estimates.

69
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:18,680
所以，为啥非得去太空？
So why space?

70
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:22,550
因为在太空，碗边能放很低，原子也不会漏。
Up there, the rim can go low without the atoms spilling out.

71
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:24,210
地球上最冷的东西，
The coldest thing on Earth

72
00:02:24,210 --> 00:02:25,670
原来在天上。
is actually up in the sky.

